    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Our main refrigerated container (reefer) for the tuna shipment from Hokkaido just reported a compressor failure while in transit. Internal temps are climbing fast and we're looking at a significant loss if we can't stabilize it. What are the immediate steps we should take to mitigate spoilage and what's the protocol for verifying if the batch is still safe for market once it arrives?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
