    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "The repair team is on site but they're saying the failure seems completely random. There was no obvious mechanical wear or external damage to the unit, it just suddenly cut out and won't reset. Is there any chance this could be an electrical issue or something that could be caused by external interference during transport?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, sudden compressor failures without visible damage can often point to control board malfunctions, sensor failures, or a tripped electrical relay. External interference, such as voltage spikes from shipyard power fluctuations or onboard electrical surges, is a possibility, especially in harsh transport conditions. The repair team should perform a thorough electrical diagnostics check to isolate whether the fault lies in the compressor itself, the power supply circuit, or the monitoring systems.",
      "source": "target",
